    headline: "Spider Vein Treatment",
    description: "Sclerotherapy for spider veins in Edmond, OK — a well-proven procedure that seals off affected veins to treat spider veins and smaller varicose veins, including associated pain and swelling.",
    heroSubhead: "Spider veins can be unsightly, but they can also cause pain or swelling in your legs. Whether you want to treat pain symptoms or simply feel confident in a skirt, sclerotherapy can help.",
    introHeading: "What Is Sclerotherapy?",
    intro: ["Spider veins form when the walls of your veins are weak and blood begins to pool inside the vein close to the skin. Sclerotherapy is a well-proven procedure that treats spider veins and smaller varicose veins by sealing off the affected vein.","Sclerotherapy is a simple procedure in which a fine needle is inserted into the affected vein. You will feel some pricks from the needle, but pain during the procedure is very mild. A session usually lasts for 30 to 45 minutes.","Our highly-trained staff will provide a thorough consultation to ensure you're a good candidate for sclerotherapy treatment."],
    signsHeading: "What This Treats",
    signsList: ["Visible spider veins on the legs","Smaller varicose veins","Leg pain associated with problem veins","Swelling in the legs","Web-like or branching surface veins","Cosmetic concern about leg appearance"],
    bullets: ["A well-proven procedure for spider veins and smaller varicose veins","Treats both the cosmetic appearance and the pain or swelling","Sessions usually last 30 to 45 minutes","Very mild discomfort — you will feel some pricks from the fine needle","Return to normal everyday activities after treatment","Thorough consultation first to confirm you are a good candidate"],
    benefits: [{"title":"Treats Symptoms, Not Just Looks","body":"Spider veins can cause genuine pain and swelling — sclerotherapy addresses both the discomfort and the appearance."},{"title":"Well-Proven Procedure","body":"Sclerotherapy is an established treatment that works by sealing off the affected vein."},{"title":"Quick Sessions","body":"A session usually lasts 30 to 45 minutes."},{"title":"Mild Discomfort","body":"A fine needle is used and pain during the procedure is very mild."},{"title":"Return to Normal Activity","body":"After treatment you can return to your normal everyday activities, and walking regularly is encouraged."},{"title":"Candidacy Assessed First","body":"A thorough consultation confirms sclerotherapy is right for you before any treatment."}],
    faqs: [{"q":"What happens during the treatment?","a":"Sclerotherapy is a simple procedure in which a fine needle is inserted into the affected vein. You will feel some pricks from the needle, but pain during the procedure is very mild. A sclerotherapy session usually lasts for 30 to 45 minutes."},{"q":"Is there downtime?","a":"After your treatment there may be a raised or red area at the injection site and you may experience some temporary itchiness. This typically subsides after a few hours, or in some cases a few days. You may need to wear compression stockings for a few weeks to compress the treated veins. You can return to your normal everyday activities, and walking regularly is recommended, especially in the days immediately following your procedure."},{"q":"How quickly will I see results?","a":"You will begin to notice the results of your sclerotherapy treatment gradually, anywhere from 4 to 8 weeks following the procedure. A few months may be required for larger veins."},{"q":"Does it work for everyone?","a":"A very small percentage of patients do not respond to sclerotherapy, and other treatment options may be recommended. Our highly-trained staff will provide a thorough consultation to ensure you're a good candidate."}],
